{
 "_comment": "Executable KDE check contracts: the FULL FSMA 204 KDE list per CTE, each mapped to the canonical customer field(s) the engine reads (satisfied_by = any-of). Fields come from the structured event/line-item sheets OR are promoted from the customer's 07_KDE_Values rows by field_key, so KDEs the workbook actually carries (source references, harvest origin) feed the check. This replaces the hardcoded KDE_CONTRACTS and is reviewable data, not code. 'required' = a real gap if absent; 'conditional' = credited when present, never failed when absent. Severity 'high' = TLC; 'medium' = other KDEs. v-bump: 2026-07-07 accuracy audit - tlc_source required on shipping/receiving (1.1340(a)(7)/1.1345(a)(7)); initial-packing TLC-source location, harvest/received date+qty (1.1330(a)); FLR receiver location (1.1335(e)); cooling harvest-farm (1.1325(b)(1)(vi)); field/container required (1.1325(a)(1)(v)/(vi)); harvester contact (1.1325(a)(2)); sprouts seed KDEs conditional (1.1330(b)). Per-input transformation detail (1.1350(a)(1)(ii)/(iii)) is enforced by the transformation_linkage lot check, not per-event KDEs. v3: transformation/cooling location KDEs also satisfied by location_id (the mapper's natural target for 'Transformation Location ID' columns) - fixes a false 'missing transformation location' on exports that carry the column. v4: cooling_location KDE also satisfied by the cooling_location slug itself (templates with a 'Cooling Site' column map there). v5: harvesting harvester_contact also satisfied by harvester_name/harvester_phone (the slugs the mapper produces for 'Crew Lead'/'Crew Phone' columns).",
